# TTP-2026-0129 — ClickFix Interpreter-Depth Loader Chain: mshta -> extrac32 CAB Unpack -> Masqueraded Signed AutoIt3 (.a3x) — Lumma Stealer ABIOC
# XQL paste-buffer generated by detection_scanner/scripts/export_artifacts.py

## ABIOC — ClickFix mshta Remote Fetch Parenting a Windows Command-Shell Loader Lineage (behavioral-ML, causality-anchored)
# severity: high
# behavioral_profile: machine-learning
# causality_anchor: User paste via RunMRU under explorer.exe -> mshta.exe remote fetch -> cmd.exe/powershell.exe loader lineage, anchored to the mshta signed-binary-proxy parent.
# A signed Microsoft mshta.exe carrying a remote/URL argument parents a cmd.exe or powershell.exe loader stage. mshta and cmd are both legitimate; the ABIOC anchors on the lineage (signed-binary-proxy remote fetch spawning an interpreter loader) rather than any known-bad string, catching the ClickFix post-paste loader hand-off that a static rule keyed on a single binary would miss.

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter actor_process_image_name = "mshta.exe"
| filter actor_process_command_line contains "http" or actor_process_command_line contains ".co/" or actor_process_command_line contains "=+"
| filter action_process_image_name in ("cmd.exe", "powershell.exe")
| comp count() as loader_spawns by agent_hostname, actor_process_command_line, action_process_image_name
| filter loader_spawns >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, actor_process_command_line, action_process_image_name, loader_spawns

## ABIOC — AV and EDR Product Discovery via tasklist Piped to findstr in a Loader Lineage (behavioral-ML, causality-anchored)
# severity: medium
# behavioral_profile: machine-learning
# causality_anchor: Loader cmd.exe/mshta.exe lineage -> tasklist -> findstr filtering on security-product process names, anchored to the loader parent.
# A cmd/mshta-parented lineage runs tasklist piped to findstr searching for security-product process names (opssvc, wrsa, bdservicehost, SophosHealth, AvastUI, AVGUI, nsWscSvc, ekrn). The commands are benign admin tools; the ABIOC fires on the security-software-discovery intent inside a loader lineage, anchored to the parent that spawned the probe.

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter action_process_image_name = "findstr.exe"
| filter action_process_command_line contains "opssvc" or action_process_command_line contains "wrsa" or action_process_command_line contains "bdservicehost" or action_process_command_line contains "SophosHealth" or action_process_command_line contains "AvastUI" or action_process_command_line contains "AVGUI" or action_process_command_line contains "nsWscSvc" or action_process_command_line contains "ekrn"
| filter causality_actor_process_image_name in ("cmd.exe", "mshta.exe", "PartyContinued.exe")
| comp count() as av_probe by agent_hostname, action_process_command_line
| filter av_probe >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, action_process_command_line, av_probe

## ABIOC — extrac32 CAB Unpack into a Masqueraded Signed AutoIt3 Interpreter Running an a3x Script (behavioral-ML, causality-anchored)
# severity: high
# behavioral_profile: machine-learning
# causality_anchor: mshta fetch -> cmd loader -> extrac32 unpack of a non-.cab archive (Boat.pst) + copy /b reconstruction -> validly-signed AutoIt3 running under a renamed image (Slovenia.com) against an .a3x script; the ABIOC requires at least TWO distinct loader stages (extrac32 unpack AND renamed signed-AutoIt3 exec) sharing one non-cmd causality owner before it groups them into a single Lumma-loader incident.
# The flagship grouping ABIOC. It requires TWO distinct loader stages under ONE non-cmd causality owner (mshta.exe / extrac32.exe / PartyContinued.exe) inside the window: extrac32.exe unpacking a Cabinet archive delivered under a benign extension AND a validly-signed AutoIt3 interpreter running under a NON-standard image name (e.g. Slovenia.com instead of autoit3.exe). Signer says AutoIt, filename does not — that masquerade PLUS a second distinct stage sharing the lineage is what the ABIOC scores (filter distinct_stages >= 2), so a lone extrac32 /E CAB extraction or a single renamed binary does NOT trip it. cmd.exe is deliberately excluded as a causality owner because it is the CGO for enormous benign volume (routine CAB extraction, legitimately compiled AutoIt tools). This is the MODEL-ONLY detection a full (destructive) detonation of the masqueraded signed AutoIt3 stage would raise; SIM-EDR-017 runs the extrac32 unpack for real but models the AutoIt3 masquerade with a SAFE-MODE marker, so the pair does not assert this grouping fires under SAFE-MODE.

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter (action_process_image_name = "extrac32.exe" and action_process_command_line contains "/E") or (action_process_signature_vendor contains "AutoIt" and action_process_image_name not in ("autoit3.exe", "autoit3_x64.exe"))
| filter causality_actor_process_image_name in ("mshta.exe", "extrac32.exe", "PartyContinued.exe")
| comp count_distinct(action_process_image_name) as distinct_stages by agent_hostname, causality_actor_process_image_name
| filter distinct_stages >= 2
| sort desc distinct_stages
| fields agent_hostname, causality_actor_process_image_name, distinct_stages

## VALIDATION — extrac32 Unpack and Renamed AutoIt3 Interpreter Execution Surfaced
# purpose: validation
# dataset: xdr_data

dataset = xdr_data
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 900)
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter action_process_image_name = "extrac32.exe" or (action_process_signature_vendor contains "AutoIt" and action_process_image_name != "autoit3.exe")
| comp count() as surfaced by agent_hostname, action_process_image_name
| filter surfaced >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, action_process_image_name, surfaced

## VALIDATION — tasklist to findstr Security-Product Discovery Command Line
# purpose: validation
# dataset: xdr_data

dataset = xdr_data
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 900)
| filter action_process_image_name in ("tasklist.exe", "findstr.exe")
| filter action_process_command_line contains "opssvc" or action_process_command_line contains "wrsa" or action_process_command_line contains "SophosHealth" or action_process_command_line contains "AvastUI"
| comp count() as probes by agent_hostname
| filter probes >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, probes

## VALIDATION — Loader Stager Fetch and Lumma C2 Egress on the Network Plane
# purpose: hunt
# dataset: network_story

dataset = network_story
| filter dst_host contains "r2.dev" or dst_host = "sumeriavgv.digital" or dst_host = "iplogger.co"
| comp count() as egress_events by agent_hostname, dst_host
| filter egress_events >= 1
| fields agent_hostname, dst_host, egress_events

